[183.124854, "o", "All commodities in the dataset:\r\n\r\n"]
[183.124908, "o", "1. Index: PALLFNF - All Commodity Price Index, 2005 = 100, includes both Fuel and Non-Fuel Price Indices\r\n2. Index.1: PNFUEL - Non-Fuel Price Index, 2005 = 100, includes Food and Beverages and Industrial Inputs Price Indices\r\n3. Index.2: PFANDB - Food and Beverage Price Index, 2005 = 100, includes Food and Beverage Price Indices\r\n"]
[183.124939, "o", "4. Index.3: PFOOD - Food Price Index, 2005 = 100, includes Cereal, Vegetable Oils, Meat, Seafood, Sugar, Bananas, and Oranges Price Indices\r\n5. Index.4: PBEVE - Beverage Price Index, 2005 = 100, includes Coffee, Tea, and Cocoa\r\n6. Index.5: PINDU - Industrial Inputs Price Index, 2005 = 100, includes Agricultural Raw Materials and Metals Price Indices\r\n7. Index.6: PRAWM - Agricultural Raw Materials Index, 2005 = 100, includes Timber, Cotton, Wool, Rubber, and Hides Price Indices\r\n"]
[183.125179, "o", "8. Index.7: PMETA - Metals Price Index, 2005 = 100, includes Copper, Aluminum, Iron Ore, Tin, Nickel, Zinc, Lead, and Uranium Price Indices\r\n9. Index.8: PNRG - Fuel (Energy) Index, 2005 = 100, includes Crude oil (petroleum), Natural Gas, and Coal Price Indices\r\n10. Index.9: POILAPSP - Crude Oil (petroleum), Price index, 2005 = 100, simple average of three spot prices; Dated Brent, West Texas Intermediate, and the Dubai Fateh\r\n11. USD: PALUM - Aluminum, 99.5% minimum purity, LME spot price, CIF UK ports, US$ per metric ton\r\n"]
[183.125278, "o", "12. USD.1: PBANSOP - Bananas, Central American and Ecuador, FOB U.S. Ports, US$ per metric ton\r\n13. USD.2: PBARL - Barley, Canadian no.1 Western Barley, spot price, US$ per metric ton\r\n14. USD.3: PBEEF - Beef, Australian and New Zealand 85% lean fores, CIF U.S. import price, US cents per pound\r\n15. USD.4: PCOALAU - Coal, Australian thermal coal, 12,000- btu/pound, less than 1% sulfur, 14% ash, FOB Newcastle/Port Kembla, US$ per metric ton\r\n16. USD.5: PCOCO - Cocoa beans, International Cocoa Organization cash price, CIF US and European ports, US$ per metric ton\r\n17. USD.6: PCOFFOTM - Coffee, Other Mild Arabicas, International Coffee Organization New York cash price, ex-dock New York, US cents per pound\r\n18. USD.7: PCOFFROB - Coffee, Robusta, International Coffee Organization New York cash price, ex-dock New York, US cents per pound\r\n19. USD.8: PROIL - Rapeseed oil, crude, fob Rotterdam, US$ per metric ton\r\n20. USD.9: PCOPP - Copper, grade A cathode, LME spot price, CIF European ports, US$ per metric ton\r\n21. USD.10: PCOTTIND - Cotton, Cotton Outlook 'A Index', Middling 1-3/32 inch staple, CIF Liverpool, US cents per pound\r\n22. USD.11: PFISH - Fishmeal, Peru Fish meal/pellets 65% protein, CIF, US$ per metric ton\r\n23. USD.12: PGNUTS - Groundnuts (peanuts), 40/50 (40 to 50 count per ounce), cif Argentina, US$ per metric ton\r\n24. USD.13: PHIDE - Hides, Heavy native steers, over 53 pounds, wholesale dealer's price, US, Chicago, fob Shipping Point, US cents per pound\r\n25. USD.14: PIORECR - China import Iron Ore Fines 62% FE spot (CFR Tianjin port), US dollars per metric ton\r\n26. USD.15: PLAMB - Lamb, frozen carcass Smithfield London, US cents per pound\r\n27. USD.16: PLEAD - Lead, 99.97% pure, LME spot price, CIF European Ports, US$ per metric ton\r\n28. USD.17: PLOGORE - Soft Logs, Average Export price from the U.S. for Douglas Fir, US$ per cubic meter\r\n29. USD.18: PLOGSK - Hard Logs, Best quality Malaysian meranti, import price Japan, US$ per cubic meter\r\n30. USD.19: PMAIZMT - Maize (corn), U.S. No.2 Yellow, FOB Gulf of Mexico, U.S. price, US$ per metric ton\r\n31. USD.20: PNGASEU - Natural Gas, Russian Natural Gas border price in Germany, US$ per Million Metric British Thermal Unit\r\n32. USD.21: PNGASJP - Natural Gas, Indonesian Liquefied Natural Gas in Japan, US$ per Million Metric British Thermal Unit\r\n33. USD.22: PNGASUS - Natural Gas, Natural Gas spot price at the Henry Hub terminal in Louisiana, US$ per Million Metric British Thermal Unit\r\n34. USD.23: PNICK - Nickel, melting grade, LME spot price, CIF European ports, US$ per metric ton\r\n35. USD.24: POILAPSP - Crude Oil (petroleum), simple average of three spot prices; Dated Brent, West Texas Intermediate, and the Dubai Fateh\r\n36. USD.25: POILBRE - Crude Oil (petroleum),  Dated Brent, light blend 38 API, fob U.K., US$ per barrel\r\n37. USD.26: POILDUB - Oil; Dubai, medium, Fateh 32 API, fob Dubai Crude Oil (petroleum), Dubai Fateh Fateh 32 API, US$ per barrel\r\n38. USD.27: POILWTI - Crude Oil (petroleum), West Texas Intermediate 40 API, Midland Texas, US$ per barrel\r\n39. USD.28: POLVOIL - Olive Oil, extra virgin less than 1% free fatty acid, ex-tanker price U.K., US$ per metric ton\r\n"]
